    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Galvin Property are delighted to introduce 87 North Circular Road to the open market for sale. No.87 is an elegant two storey over garden level period residence offering huge potential. The property is located on a lovely tree lined section of the North Circular Road close to Phibsboro village and Grangegorman.  This fine property provides wonderful accommodation and retains many period features throughout including fireplaces, high ornate ceilings and cornicing to name just a few. \r\n\r\nApproached by its original granite steps, the property extends to circa 275sqm (2,960sqft).  At garden (basement) level, a self contained property comprising hallway, 3 bedrooms (one ensuite), living/dining room, kitchen, utility and bathroom. The upper floors comprise of a hallway, living room, dining room, family room and WC. The upper floor comprises four bedrooms and a family bathroom. There is a staircase connecting the garden level to the first floor level which has been closed off but can easily be opened to allow for one large family home. The rear garden can be accessed from both garden and first floor level. To the front, the garden is bordered by wrought-iron railing. \r\n\r\nThe North Circular Road is a truly convenient location, ideally positioned within a gentle stroll to all of the amenities that Dublin 7 has to offer. Commuting to the city centre is a leisurely stroll and there are many bus routes passing on the North Circular road along with the Luas stops at Phibsborough and Grangegorman. The New DIT campus at Grangegorman and the Phoenix Park are literally on your doorstep along with numerous national and secondary schools all within easy reach.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to appreciate the potential this property has to offer. Call us now on 01 4964612 to arrange a viewing."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Superb Dublin 7 location\r\nSubstantial property with considerable potential to extend/convert (subject to planning permission)\r\nProperty will suit both homeowners & investors\r\nBeautiful period property built c. late 1800s with many original features\r\nWalking distance to the wonderful Phoenix Park and Dublin City Centre\r\nExcellent choice of local national and secondary schools"
      },
      {
